"Sampling Algorithms and Coresets for Lp Regression (https://arxiv.org/abs/0707.1714)\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 19.3 years ago; Title: Sampling Algorithms and Coresets for Lp RegressionAuthors: Anirban Dasgupta, Petros Drineas, Boulos Harb, Ravi Kumar, Michael W. ... The first stage of our algorithm non-uniformly samples $\\hat{r}_1 = O(36^p d^{\\max\\{p/2+1, p\\}+1})$ rows of $A$ and the corresponding elements of $b$, and then it solves the Lp regression problem on the sample; we prove this is an 8-approximation.\nTitle: Sampling Algorithms and Coresets for Lp Regression\nAuthors: Anirban Dasgupta, Petros Drineas, Boulos Harb, Ravi Kumar, Michael W. Mahoney\nDate: Wed Jul 11 22:04:18 2007\n\nThe Lp regression problem takes as input a matrix $A \\in \\Real^{n \\times d}$, a vector $b \\in \\Real^n$, and a number $p \\in [1,\\infty)$, and it returns as output a number ${\\cal Z}$ and a vector $x_{opt} \\in \\Real^d$ such that ${\\cal Z} = \\min_{x \\in \\Real^d} ||Ax -b||_p = ||Ax_{opt}-b||_p$. In this paper, we construct coresets and obtain an efficient two-stage sampling-based approximation algorithm for the very overconstrained ($n \\gg d$) version of this classical problem, for all $p \\in [1, \\infty)$. The first stage of our algorithm non-uniformly samples $\\hat{r}_1 = O(36^p d^{\\max\\{p/2+1, p\\}+1})$ rows of $A$ and the corresponding elements of $b$, and then it solves the Lp regression problem on the sample; we prove this is an 8-approximation. The second stage of our algorithm uses the output of the first stage to resample $\\hat{r}_1/\\epsilon^2$ constraints, and then it solves the Lp regression problem on the new sample; we prove this is a $(1+\\epsilon)$-approximation. Our algorithm unifies, improves upon, and extends the existing algorithms for special cases of Lp regression, namely $p = 1,2$. In course of proving our result, we develop two concepts--well-conditioned bases and subspace-preserving sampling--that are of independent interest.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Proportional Uap Characterizes Weak Hilbert Spaces - Johnson - 1991 - Journal of the London Mathematical Society - Wiley Online Library (https://londmathsoc.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdfdirect/10.1112/jlms/s2-44.3.525)\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 34.9 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; # The Proportional Uap Characterizes Weak Hilbert Spaces ... Johnson, ... We prove that a Banach space has the uniform approximation property with proportional growth of the uniformity function if and only if it is a weak Hilbert space.\n\nVolume s2-44, Issue 3 pp. 525-536\n\nNotes and papers\n\n# The Proportional Uap Characterizes Weak Hilbert Spaces\n\nW. B. Johnson, \n\nW. B. Johnson\n\nTexas A&M University, College Station, Texas 77843-3368, USA e-mail: WBJ7835@tamvenus\n\nSearch for more papers by this author\n\nG. Pisier, \n\nG. Pisier\n\nTexas A&M University, College Station, Texas 77843-3368, USA e-mail: GJP1168@tamvenus and Equipe d'Analyse, Université Paris VI, 75230 Paris, France e-mail: GIP@frunip62\n\nSearch for more papers by this author\n\nW. B. Johnson, \n\nW. B. Johnson\n\nTexas A&M University, College Station, Texas 77843-3368, USA e-mail: WBJ7835@tamvenus\n\nSearch for more papers by this author\n\nG. Pisier, \n\nG. Pisier\n\nTexas A&M University, College Station, Texas 77843-3368, USA e-mail: GJP1168@tamvenus and Equipe d'Analyse, Université Paris VI, 75230 Paris, France e-mail: GIP@frunip62\n\nSearch for more papers by this author\n\nFirst published: December 1991\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1112/jlms/s2-44.3.525Digital Object Identifier (DOI)\n\n### Abstract\n\nWe prove that a Banach space has the uniform approximation property with proportional growth of the uniformity function if and only if it is a weak Hilbert space.\n\n## \n\nCiting Literature\n\nVolumes2-44, Issue3\n\nDecember 1991\n\nPages 525-536\n\n### Details\n\n© 1991 London Mathematical Socie